{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And every terumah, etc.</b> Rabbi Yishmael said: Now does one offer terumah to the priest? Is it not he who goes after it to the granary? Then what does Scripture tell, 'that they offer to the priest'? These are the first fruits, of which it is said (Exodus 23), ״תָּבִיא בֵּית ה' אֱלֹהֶיךָ״ — and I do not know what is done with them; Scripture tells, 'to the priest, to him it shall be' — the verse comes and teaches about the first fruits that they are given to the priest. (Sifrei)"], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:26.291710994Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}